      "side": 1,
      "message": "At long last, I think I have identified the cause of occasional crashes on STM32L5xx.  This chip belongs to the Cortex-M33 architecture, which apparently uses additional possible values for EXC_RETURN beyond what M0 and M4 did.",
      "revId": "0c1c4fe538fd2ecd231c53ecd7858fadacadd6cc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92a2c623_ae37b504",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 392,
